---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Support — Clear North"
  description="Help with Clear North: Aurora Alerts — why you did or did not get an alert, stale data, notifications, red mode, and subscriptions."
>
  <div class="cn">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container support-content">
      <span class="section-label">// clear north</span>
      <h1>Support</h1>
      <p>Send a note with your iPhone model, iOS version, roughly where you are, and the night in question. That is usually enough to work out what happened.</p>
      <a href="mailto:matt@mattdonders.com?subject=Clear%20North%20Support" class="btn btn-primary">Email Support</a>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>

      <h3>Why did I get an alert?</h3>
      <p>Clear North alerts only when three things are true at once for your area: it is astronomical darkness, cloud cover is under 40% (MET Norway), and the Kp index is high enough for your latitude (NOAA SWPC), for example Kp 6+ at 45&deg;N. If you turned on &ldquo;wake me for major storms,&rdquo; a Kp 7+ storm can also come through as a time-sensitive notification.</p>

      <h3>Why did I not get an alert when the aurora was out?</h3>
      <p>Usually one of the three conditions was not met: it was not fully dark yet, the forecast showed 40% cloud or more, or Kp was below your latitude&rsquo;s threshold. Your nightly limit (default 2) may already have been used, and quiet hours suppress ordinary alerts. Also check that alerts are on, that you have Clear North Pro, and that notifications are allowed for the app. Forecasts can be wrong, and the aurora sometimes shows when the numbers say it should not; Clear North is a guide, not a guarantee.</p>

      <h3>The data looks stale.</h3>
      <p>Cloud forecasts come from MET Norway and Kp comes from NOAA SWPC, and both update on their own schedules. If the app cannot reach them it shows the last data it received. Check your connection, pull to refresh, and try again in a few minutes. Space weather can change quickly, so a forecast that is a few hours old may no longer be accurate.</p>

      <h3>I am not getting any notifications.</h3>
      <p>Open iOS Settings, then Notifications, then Clear North, and make sure notifications are allowed. Check that no Focus mode is silencing them, that alerts are turned on inside the app, and that the current time is not inside your quiet hours. Time-sensitive delivery for major storms also depends on your Focus settings.</p>

      <h3>What is red mode?</h3>
      <p>Red night-vision mode switches the display to red so it does not ruin your dark-adapted eyes while you are watching the sky.</p>

      <h3>How do I cancel my subscription?</h3>
      <p>Subscriptions are managed by Apple. Open iOS Settings, tap your name, then Subscriptions, choose Clear North Pro, and cancel. If you are in the 7-day free trial, cancel at least 24 hours before it ends to avoid being charged. Deleting the app does not cancel a subscription.</p>

      <h3>I bought Pro but it is not unlocked.</h3>
      <p>Use Restore Purchases in the app, signed in to the same Apple Account you used to buy it.</p>

      <h3>Refunds</h3>
      <p>Purchases are handled by Apple. Refund requests go through <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.</p>

      <h3>How do I delete my data?</h3>
      <p>Turn alerts off in the app, which deletes your device record from our server. You can also email us and we will delete it. See the <a href="/apps/clear-north/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>Data sources</h2>
      <p>Cloud forecasts: <a href="https://api.met.no/">MET Norway</a>, licensed <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. Geomagnetic data: <a href="https://www.swpc.noaa.gov/">NOAA Space Weather Prediction Center</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .cn {
    --bg: #080b14;
    --surface: #10141f;
    --border: #232a3b;
    --text: #ece6d8;
    --text-muted: #b4aea0;
    --accent: #86e8b0;
    --accent-hover: #a8f0c6;
    --accent-dim: rgba(134, 232, 176, 0.1);
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .cn h1, .cn h2 { font-family: 'Newsreader', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; font-weight: 500; }
  .cn .btn-primary { color: #080b14; }
  .support-content { max-width: 700px; }
  .support-content h2 { margin-top: 3rem; }
  .support-content h3 { margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .support-content p { margin-bottom: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; }
</style>
